<title>USA: Live Entertainment completes merger.</title>
<headline>Live Entertainment completes merger.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Live Entertainment Inc Thursday said its merger with an investment group led by Richland Gordon &amp; Co has been completed on the previously announced terms.</p>
<p>As of July 11, Live's common stock and Series B preferred stock will no longer be listed.</p>
<p>Live shareholders will receive $6.00 a share, and holders of the Series B preferred will receive $100 per share plus accrued and unpaid dividends through the closing date.</p>
<p>Series C preferred stockholders will receive $944.8624 a share.</p>
<p>Live will redeem its increasing rate secured senior subordinated notes, due 1999, as of August 8.</p>
<p>Live specializes in motion picture marketing and distribution in the United States and other countries.</p>
</text>
